xnu 0117: read the touch pins the bootloader left

The panel's touch part is a Goodix on QUPv3 SE4, with reset on TLMM GPIO20,
IRQ on GPIO21 and AVDD enable on GPIO71; its IOVDD is the RPMh rail
pm8350c_l2. Driving any of that needs the TLMM first, so start by reading:
the probe prints CFG/IN_OUT/INTR_CFG/INTR_STATUS for the three pins once the
log thread is running, one single-page mapping per pin (an 18 MB ml_io_map
has failed on this board), with a ring flush before each read so a fault
leaves the last line on disk.

The pin registers are at 0x0f100000 + 0x1000*n, not at the 0x0f000000 of the
live tree's pinctrl node: that node's 16 MB region starts with a 1 MB hole,
and reading 0x0f014000 wedges the interconnect (no abort, no more timer
interrupts, watchdog reset). Mainline's pinctrl-sm8450 uses 0x0f100000.

Reading only is deliberate: it says how the bootloader left the pins and
whether the rail is up before anything writes to the PMIC or the pads.

--- a/bsd/conf/files
+++ b/bsd/conf/files
@@ -106,6 +106,7 @@
 bsd/dev/memdev.c			standard
 bsd/dev/mondrian_ufs.c			standard
 bsd/dev/mondrian_sample.c		standard
+bsd/dev/mondrian_touch.c		standard
 bsd/dev/mem.c				standard
 bsd/dev/munge.c 			optional config_requires_u32_munging
 bsd/dev/unix_startup.c			standard
--- a/bsd/dev/mondrian_ufs.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/mondrian_ufs.c
@@ -1483,6 +1483,16 @@
 		printf("MONDRIAN LOG: writer thread started\n");
 	} else {
 		printf("MONDRIAN LOG: writer thread start failed (%d)\n", kr);
+	}
